CH = dict(num=11, tag="Maths", title="Areas Related to Circles", theme="Circumference and area, sector, segment, combinations of plane figures",
intro="A pizza slice, the sweep of a windscreen wiper, a lawn watered by a rotating sprinkler and a running track all involve parts of circles. This chapter recalls the circumference and area of a circle and extends them to sectors and segments, then uses them for areas of shapes made by combining squares, triangles and circles.",
big_questions=["How are the area and length of a sector or arc related to the whole circle?", "How is the area of a segment found?", "How do we find areas of combined or shaded figures?"],
blocks=[
("h2", "11.1 Circle: Revision"),
("note", "FORMULA", "**Circumference = 2&pi;r = &pi;d.  Area = &pi;r<sup>2</sup>.**  Use &pi; = 22/7 when the radius is a multiple of 7, otherwise 3.14, unless stated. **Semicircle:** area &pi;r<sup>2</sup>/2, perimeter &pi;r + 2r. **Ring (annulus)** between radii R and r: area = &pi;(R<sup>2</sup> &minus; r<sup>2</sup>)."),
("p", "**Examples.** A wheel of diameter 70 cm has circumference 220 cm, so it makes 110000/220 = **500 revolutions** in 1.1 km. A ring between circles of radii 14 cm and 7 cm has area (22/7)(196 &minus; 49) = **462 cm<sup>2</sup>**. If the circumference is 44 cm, then r = 7 cm and area = 154 cm<sup>2</sup>."),
("h2", "11.2 Sector and Arc"),
("note", "DEFINITION", "A **sector** is the region bounded by two radii and the arc between them. The smaller one is the **minor sector** and the larger the **major sector** (angle &theta; and 360&deg; &minus; &theta;)."),
("note", "FORMULA", "For a sector of angle **&theta; (in degrees)** and radius r:  **Length of arc = (&theta;/360) x 2&pi;r.**  **Area of sector = (&theta;/360) x &pi;r<sup>2</sup> = (1/2) x arc length x r.**  **Perimeter of sector = 2r + arc length.**"),
("table", ["Radius", "Angle", "Arc length", "Area of sector"], [["6 cm", "60&deg;", "2&pi; = 6.28 cm", "6&pi; = 18.86 cm<sup>2</sup>"], ["14 cm", "90&deg;", "22 cm", "154 cm<sup>2</sup>"], ["5 cm", "72&deg;", "2&pi; = 6.28 cm", "5&pi; = 15.7 cm<sup>2</sup>"], ["21 cm", "120&deg;", "44 cm", "462 cm<sup>2</sup>"]]),
("p", "**Clock example.** The minute hand of a clock is 14 cm long. In 5 minutes it turns 30&deg;, so the area swept is (30/360)(22/7)(14)<sup>2</sup> = **154/3 = 51.33 cm<sup>2</sup>**; the tip travels 22/3 = 7.33 cm. In 1 hour the tip travels 2&pi;r = 88 cm."),
("h2", "11.3 Segment of a Circle"),
("note", "DEFINITION", "A **segment** is the region between a chord and the arc. The smaller is the **minor segment**; the other is the **major segment**."),
("note", "FORMULA", "**Area of minor segment = area of sector &minus; area of triangle OAB** = (&theta;/360)&pi;r<sup>2</sup> &minus; (1/2)r<sup>2</sup> sin &theta;.  **Area of major segment = &pi;r<sup>2</sup> &minus; area of minor segment.**  For &theta; = 90&deg;, the triangle has area r<sup>2</sup>/2; for &theta; = 60&deg; it is equilateral with area (&radic;3/4)r<sup>2</sup>; for &theta; = 120&deg; the triangle area is (&radic;3/4)r<sup>2</sup> too."),
("p", "**Example.** A chord subtends 90&deg; at the centre of a circle of radius 10 cm. Sector = (1/4)(3.14)(100) = 78.5; triangle = (1/2)(10)(10) = 50; **minor segment = 28.5 cm<sup>2</sup>**, major segment = 314 &minus; 28.5 = 285.5 cm<sup>2</sup>. **60&deg; segment of radius 6 cm:** sector 6&pi; = 18.84; triangle (&radic;3/4) x 36 = 15.57; segment = **3.27 cm<sup>2</sup>**."),
("h2", "11.4 Combinations of Plane Figures"),
("steps", [("Step 1", "Break the figure into squares, rectangles, triangles, sectors and segments."), ("Step 2", "Add or subtract the areas depending on whether the part is included or removed (shaded region = outer figure &minus; unshaded parts)."), ("Step 3", "Identify radii and angles from the figure, particularly equal arcs and quarter-circles.")]),
("table", ["Figure", "Area / perimeter"], [["Square of side 14 cm with four quarter circles of radius 7 cm at its corners removed", "196 &minus; 154 = **42 cm<sup>2</sup>**"], ["Running track: rectangle with a semicircle at each end", "rectangle + &pi;r<sup>2</sup>; perimeter = 2l + 2&pi;r"], ["Circle inscribed in a square of side a", "Area = &pi;a<sup>2</sup>/4, shaded corners = a<sup>2</sup>(1 &minus; &pi;/4)"], ["Square inscribed in a circle of radius r", "Side = r&radic;2; area of square 2r<sup>2</sup>; circle left over = (&pi; &minus; 2)r<sup>2</sup>"]]),
("p", "**Example.** A horse is tied with a 5 m rope at a corner of a square field: it can graze the quarter circle (1/4)(3.14)(25) = **19.63 m<sup>2</sup>**. If the rope is 10 m, the quarter circle gives 78.5 m<sup>2</sup>."),
("note", "IMPORTANT", "Use the angle in **degrees** in the sector formulas. When the question says 'minor' or 'major', check the angle; if the angle of the sector is not given, find it from the chord using triangle properties."),
("h2", "Quick Revision: Likely Exam Questions"),
("qa", [("Write the area of a sector of angle &theta;.", "(&theta;/360) x &pi;r<sup>2</sup>."), ("Length of the arc of a sector of angle 60&deg; and radius 21 cm?", "22 cm."), ("What is a segment?", "The region between a chord and the arc."), ("Area of a ring between radii 7 and 5?", "&pi;(49 &minus; 25) = 24&pi; = 75.43 cm<sup>2</sup> (with &pi; = 22/7)."), ("Perimeter of a quadrant of radius 7?", "11 + 14 = 25 cm."), ("How is a minor segment's area found?", "Sector area minus triangle area."), ("How many times does a wheel of radius 35 cm revolve in 22 m?", "22/2.2 = 10."), ("Area of a semicircle with diameter 14 cm?", "77 cm<sup>2</sup>.")]),
],
takeaways=["**Arc = (&theta;/360) 2&pi;r; sector = (&theta;/360) &pi;r<sup>2</sup>.**", "**Minor segment = sector &minus; triangle**; major segment = circle &minus; minor segment.", "Shaded area = **total area &minus; unshaded parts** (or sum of parts).", "Wheel problems: **distance = number of turns x circumference**."])
